.TH MAPS-VIDEO-EVENT-RECORDER 1 "21 September 2026" "maps-apps 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
maps-video-event-recorder \- create event-centred MediaMTX clips and publish S3 URLs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B maps-video-event-recorder
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B maps-video-event-recorder
subscribes to a generic MQTT recording-request topic, waits until the requested post-event
interval has elapsed, downloads an MP4 clip from the MediaMTX playback service, uploads the
clip to private Amazon S3 storage, and publishes a generic MQTT result containing a
presigned HTTPS URL.
.PP
The recorder is protocol agnostic.  It does not contain STANAG 4817 or other tasking
protocol logic.
.SH REQUIRED OPTIONS
Options can also be supplied with the corresponding environment variables.
.TP
.BI --mqtt-url " URL"
MQTT broker URL.
.TP
.BI --mediamtx-url " URL"
MediaMTX playback HTTP endpoint, for example http://127.0.0.1:9996.
.TP
.BI --s3-bucket " BUCKET"
Private destination S3 bucket.
.TP
.BI --s3-region " REGION"
AWS region containing the bucket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --request-topic " TOPIC"
Request topic. Default: maps/video/record/request.
.TP
.BI --result-topic " TOPIC"
Result topic. Default: maps/video/record/result.
.TP
.BI --qos " N"
MQTT QoS, 0 through 2. Default: 1.
.TP
.BI --before-seconds " N"
Default number of seconds before event time. Default: 30.
.TP
.BI --after-seconds " N"
Default number of seconds after event time. Default: 60.
.TP
.BI --settle-seconds " N"
Additional delay before querying MediaMTX. Default: 2.
.TP
.BI --dedupe-retention-seconds " N"
Duplicate-suppression retention. Default: 1800.
.TP
.BI --url-validity-seconds " N"
Presigned S3 URL validity. Default: 86400; maximum: 604800.
.TP
.BI --s3-prefix " PREFIX"
S3 object-key prefix. Default: detections.
.TP
.BI --mqtt-username " USER"
Optional MQTT username.
.TP
.BI --mqtt-password " PASSWORD"
Optional MQTT password.
.TP
.BI --mediamtx-username " USER"
Optional MediaMTX playback username.
.TP
.BI --mediamtx-password " PASSWORD"
Optional MediaMTX playback password.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_MQTT_URL
MQTT broker URL.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_MQTT_USERNAME
Optional MQTT username.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_MQTT_PASSWORD
Optional MQTT password.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_REQUEST_TOPIC
Request topic.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_RESULT_TOPIC
Result topic.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_QOS
MQTT QoS.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_MEDIAMTX_URL
MediaMTX playback endpoint.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_MEDIAMTX_USERNAME
Optional MediaMTX username.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_MEDIAMTX_PASSWORD
Optional MediaMTX password.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_S3_BUCKET
Destination bucket.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_S3_REGION
AWS region.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_S3_PREFIX
Object-key prefix.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_BEFORE_SECONDS
Default pre-event interval.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_AFTER_SECONDS
Default post-event interval.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_DEDUPE_RETENTION_SECONDS
Duplicate-retention period.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_URL_VALIDITY_SECONDS
Presigned URL lifetime.
.TP
.B MAPS_VIDEO_SETTLE_SECONDS
Additional MediaMTX settle delay.
.SH AWS CREDENTIALS
AWS credentials are resolved using the standard AWS SDK default credential provider chain.
Access keys are not configured by this application.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/maps/apps/video_event_recorder.jar
Executable installed by the maps-apps Debian package.
